From a92ef00db9c6eea956bfe3938c19bbbd0ff2baeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cesar carlos <cesar_carlos@msn.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 21:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(events): serialize websocket writes per connection

gorilla/websocket allows only one concurrent writer. CallWebhook runs in
a goroutine per event, so Produce() could WriteJSON the same Conn from
multiple goroutines under load (HistorySync/Receipts) and panic, killing
the whole process.

Wrap each Conn in wsConn with a write mutex so RLock still protects the
client maps while writes are serialized per connection.

Closes #99

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 pkg/events/websocket/websocket_producer.go    |  30 +++-
 .../websocket/websocket_producer_test.go      | 154 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 175 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/events/websocket/websocket_producer_test.go

